<Layout title="SAGE Financial Planning | RIPL Wealth" description="SAGE is RIPL’s paid financial planning and consulting service for business owners. Organize your business and personal finances and build a practical plan for your goals.">
<section class="hero sage-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">SAGE · PAID FINANCIAL PLANNING &amp; CONSULTING</div><h1>You have a plan for your business.<br/><span class="sage-hero-highlight">Let’s build one for your financial life.</span></h1><p class="lead">SAGE is our paid planning and consulting service for business owners who want to organize their financial lives and get their goals on track. Through four focused conversations, we connect your business and personal finances, clarify your priorities, and build a practical plan for what comes next.</p><a class="text-link sage-included-link" href="#sage-included">See What’s Included ↓</a></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2 class="sage-money-question">What do you want your money to do for you?</h2></div><div><p class="lead">We start with your life.</p><p>Before a portfolio or a product, we want to understand the life you’re building. Your business, family, commitments, and goals belong in the same conversation.</p><p>SAGE brings those conversations into a practical priority plan. You’ll understand what we’re doing, why it matters, and what comes next.</p></div></div></section><section class="section sage-steps-section" id="sage-included"><div class="wrap"><div class="sage-steps-intro"><h2>Four Straightforward Conversations.<br/>One Simple Plan You Can Act On.</h2><p>Here’s what we cover together, and what you take away from each conversation.</p></div><ol class="sage-steps"><li class="sage-step"><span class="sage-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="sage-step-card"><div class="eyebrow">CONVERSATION 1</div><h3>Vision, Goals, and Team</h3><p>Define what financial freedom means for you. Explore the stages you’re in and the decisions in front of you. Understand who already helps with your taxes, legal matters, and financial life.</p><p class="sage-step-takeaway"><strong>What you leave with</strong>A clear picture of your goals, priorities, and advisory team.</p></div></li><li class="sage-step"><span class="sage-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="sage-step-card"><div class="eyebrow">CONVERSATION 2</div><h3>Financial Flow and Foundational Security</h3><p>Map how money moves through your life. Review reserves, income needs, insurance, estate planning, and business or concentration risks that could interrupt your goals.</p><p class="sage-step-takeaway"><strong>What you leave with</strong>A view of your cash flow, reserves, and the risks worth addressing.</p></div></li><li class="sage-step"><span class="sage-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="sage-step-card"><div class="eyebrow">CONVERSATION 3</div><h3>Asset Alignment</h3><p>Look at what you own and what each asset is supposed to do. Connect business equity, cash, retirement accounts, and investments to the same goals and timelines.</p><p class="sage-step-takeaway"><strong>What you leave with</strong>A clearer purpose for your assets, connected to your goals and timelines.</p></div></li><li class="sage-step"><span class="sage-step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="sage-step-card"><div class="eyebrow">CONVERSATION 4</div><h3>Value Maximization and Plan Confirmation</h3><p>Narrow the work to three to five priorities that matter most this year. Discuss the options, the tradeoffs, and execution. Leave with a one-page priority plan and written summary.</p><p class="sage-step-takeaway"><strong>What you leave with</strong>A one-page priority plan and written summary, with three to five priorities for the year.</p></div></li></ol></div></section><section class="section questions sage-closing"><div class="wrap"><h2>Let’s get your financial life organized.</h2><p class="lead">Start with a conversation about what you want to accomplish. We’ll explain how SAGE can help, what your engagement would include, and what it costs before you decide.</p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start the Conversation →</a></div></section>
